    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advanced evidence based, effective and feasible legislative and/or regulatory measures for the 5 main NCDs risk factors. By end 2022.

Advanced whole-of-government and whole-of-society response to NCDs including stewardship and accountability. By end 2022.

Established participatory and transparent multi-stakeholder platforms and partnership for implementing the Healthy cities concept through population-wide response and engaging all relevant stakeholders. By end 2022.

Strengthened national NCD strategy and/or coordination mechanism. By end 2022.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">NCDs place a significant health and development burden on Uganda. Uganda requires urgent support in national governance and financing to address NCDs, including through prevention and in the context of COVID-19.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Review national NCD strategy
Support strengthening of national NCD coordination mechanism
NCD whole of society policy dialogue review
Parliamentarian briefing on addressing NCDs
Engage Alliance of Mayors for Healthy Cities Initiative</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">National NCD strategy review initiated
