    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Review multisectoral plan for NCDs 
 NDC multisectoral committee functional.
 NDC integrated into PEPFAR country Operations Plan (COP2022) 
 NCD advocacy strategy developed for parliament
 Re-establishment and orientation of the NCD multisectoral Coordination Committee
 62 members of parliament were trained and oriented on prevention and control/management of NCDs
 Re-establishment of the parliamentary NCD forum
 270 Urban Local Government leaders including Mayors, Town Clerks and Health Focal Persons oriented on NCDs.
 Review of Public Health Amendment Bill supported
 1 million people reached through media</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; Finalised review of the Multisectoral plan for NCDs. UNDP is supporting the functionality of the NCD multisectoral Committee. 
&#x2022; UNDP facilitated NCD integration into PEPFAR country Operations Plan 2022 (COP22) 
&#x2022; UNDP contributed to the development of NCD advocacy strategy for parliament. The strategy will facilitate future legislative prevention and control of NCDs.
&#x2022; UNDP supported re-establishment and orientation of the NCD multisectoral Coordination Committee
&#x2022; More than 62 members of parliament were trained and oriented on prevention and control/management of NCDs. 
&#x2022; UNDP supported re-establishment of the parliamentary NCD forum. The forum provides policy and legislative leadership in parliament. 
&#x2022; More than 270 Urban Local Government leaders including Mayors, Town Clerks and Health Focal Persons were oriented on NCDs. These were from nine (9) cities of Uganda including Kampala, Jinja, Masaka, Arua, Gulu, Mbale, Mbarara, Soroti and Lira 
&#x2022; UNDP supported the review of Public Health Amendment Bill. The bill was passed by Parliament and its before the executive. 
&#x2022; Through media engagement, two million people were sensitised through various media reports on NCDs</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
